  "notes": "Modified cash basis village. Governmental receipts/disbursements from the Total Governmental Funds column (p4); Loan proceeds 355,000 is printed among revenues, so it is a receipt line (category Loan Proceeds). Fund balance roll-forward 214,102 + 783,073 - 455,695 + 160,751 - 449,121 = 253,110 (ties). No cash roll-forward printed: ending_cash = governmental funds Cash 224,456 (p3), certificates of deposit 21,309 in ending_investments; county treasurer's balances 7,345 is a separate line (as FY2023); beginning cash not printed (null). Business-type from the proprietary funds modified cash statement Total column (p6), by cost type; nonoperating loan payment/interest/fee recorded as debt service disbursements (as FY2023); roll-forward -38,405 + 159,217 - 291,964 + 288,370 = 117,218 (ties); total expenditures 291,964 printed on the Statement of Activities (p2). Balance sheet: governmental lines from the governmental funds statement (totals equal government-wide 253,110), business-type lines from the Statement of Net Position business-type column (p1); the proprietary funds statement (p5) prints restricted 11,131 / unrestricted 106,087 while p1 prints 11,071 / 106,147 (same total 117,218); p1 figures used. Detail: the only supplementary schedule is the all-funds budget comparison (p7), so detail is one line per fund column of the governmental funds statement (General, Street; p4) and the proprietary funds statement (Water, Sewer; p6), per the per-fund rule; the all-funds budget schedule is not recorded. Street Fund intergovernmental kept as other state aid (highway allocation not printed). Read pages 1-7 of 7"
